35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Jonathan, the ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed! @Toshio, bank statements reveal many members struggle to pay upfront. We need flexible options!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, that fixed cost is a heavy anchor. @Takumi, the turnout drop confirms my fears. We must protect the sense of belonging.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, the numbers are brutal. A quarter of us do two-thirds of the work. Eighteen people never show up. This isn’t fair.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the ledger confirms fixed costs dominate. @Takumi, the hours show individual collection is inefficient. We need a system that reduces that burden.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, nine people left because a whole year felt too big! Eleven mid-year joiners needed hand-worked math. We need a simpler, flexible way in!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, nine people left? That’s huge! @Toshio, if fixed costs are seventy percent, we can’t just lower the fee. We need to cover that base!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, I understand the financial pressure. But @Takumi, the data shows people hesitate when they feel they must earn their place. We need to soften that barrier.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, it’s not about earning a place. It’s about the same nine people doing everything while others vanish. We need to fix the workload, not just the price.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the hours confirm the burden. @Mio, fixed costs are immovable. We need a structure that minimizes administrative time while covering that base.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I get it. But if people can’t afford the jump, they won’t show up at all. We need a low entry point to keep the doors open!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, if fixed costs are seventy percent, we can’t just lower the fee. We need to cover that base!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, the fixed costs are real, but so is the hesitation. We need a structure that feels like belonging, not a transaction.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, I hear you. But if eighteen people vanish, we can’t cover costs. We need a tiered fee based on actual attendance, not just a flat rate.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, attendance-based fees increase administrative complexity. @Mio, we must cover the fixed base. A simple, low-maintenance collection method is essential to prevent burnout.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I agree! But @Takumi, if fees change by attendance, newcomers feel judged. Let’s keep the entry simple so people can just drift in and find their feet.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Takumi, tiered fees sound messy! @Toshio, I agree, keep it simple. We need a flat rate that covers the fixed costs, maybe with monthly options?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, a flat rate feels like a transaction. @Takumi, let’s find a middle ground that preserves belonging without punishing absence.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, flat rates punish the nine who carry everything. @Toshio, if we don’t fix the workload, the fee is just a tax on the active.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
